  <XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x1143">
    <title>[PATCH] Start in 2nd</title>
    <description>Start in 2nd. Zeros the pair-0 1->2 up line and the 2->1 down line (up + 0x1E) of all 23 shift characteristics: 46 slots x 15 u16 BE = 1380 bytes, so the box pulls away and holds in 2nd. R1 on-car: still D1 at standstill (the strategy clamps the request). R2: 00 over 0x1D33D8/0x1D33E5/0x1D3419 (program/global byte 8); no on-car change. R3: 00 x13 over the global inhibit vector 0x1D3411..0x1D341D (mask/debd 0 everywhere); 0x1D341E stays stock. APPLY ORDER: Stage 3 maps first, then this as pure overwrite (no basedata); recompute the CRC after all patches. R4: adds 01 over 0x1D3A4F (stock 02), min-gear floor byte. R5: floor off + availability (e_work/notes/m1_floor_cal.md sec.5): 0x1D3A4F 01->02 (floor off, manual M1 back), 0x1CD938 0001->0002 and the 45 car-2nd min-speed words zeroed, so car 2nd is available at 0 speed (R1 request passes).</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="1" />
