  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1177" flags="0x0">
    <title>shift_element_pair_b</title>
    <description>@0x1caf14 (file +0x4ad14). Third of the three 12-byte pair tables at 0x1CAEFC / 0x1CAF08 / 0x1CAF14: 6 u16, each holding a duplicated byte. Cells: 0x0202-&gt;0x0101, 0x0202-&gt;0x0101, 0x0202-&gt;0x0303, 0x0202-&gt;0x0404, 0x0505-&gt;0x0404, 0x0505-&gt;0x0404. The tune rewrites all six to 0x0101 0x0101 0x0303 0x0404 0x0404 0x0404 - equal to the 0x1CAF08 sibling - consistent with the per-gear shift element pair list of the label evidence. The map candidate at 0x1CAF18 (auto_1caf18: x/y breakpoints are bytes of this table, z = 4x10000 at 0x1CAF22) reads the same bytes differently and is dropped; its z bytes are not edited, so no coverage is lost. Confidence MED.</description>
